# Disease Prediction — Breast Cancer Classification

Predicts whether a breast tumor is benign or malignant using the UCI Breast Cancer Wisconsin (Original) dataset. Compares Logistic Regression, Random Forest, and SVM classifiers.

## Dataset
- [UCI Breast Cancer Wisconsin (Original)](https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/15/breast+cancer+wisconsin+original) — 699 samples, 9 features
- Fetched via `ucimlrepo`; missing values imputed with median

## Pipeline
1. Clean & impute data
2. Encode labels (benign=0, malignant=1)
3. 80/20 stratified train/test split + `StandardScaler`
4. Train Logistic Regression, Random Forest, SVM
5. Evaluate with accuracy, precision, recall, F1, confusion matrix, ROC/AUC

## Results

| Model | Accuracy | Precision | Recall | F1 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Logistic Regression | 0.950 | 0.936 | 0.917 | 0.926 |
| Random Forest | 0.950 | 0.918 | 0.938 | 0.928 |
| **SVM (best)** | **0.957** | **0.938** | **0.938** | **0.938** |


## Note
For educational purposes only — not for clinical use.
